  "notes": [
    "Partial encoding of Alaska Medicaid Imcivree (setmelanotide). Version 2; Original: 2/27/2021; Updated: 12/23/2025; Effective: 03/01/2026.",
    "Closed indications attest to diagnosis. Indication-specific approval gates and shared denial exclusions are encoded. Weight eligibility selects attest to the entire age/weight branch; numeric weight, BMI and percentile verification require manual review. Source age bands 6–17 and 2–6 overlap at age 6 and are preserved as written. FDA indications describe deficiency variants determined by an FDA-approved test.",
    "Cautions (notes only): monitor disturbances in sexual arousal, depression and suicidal ideation; generalized increased skin pigmentation and darkening of pre-existing nevi may occur. Benzyl alcohol-preserved drugs can cause serious and fatal reactions including gasping syndrome in neonates and low birth weight infants.",
    "Duration (notes only): initial approval up to 3 months; reauthorization up to 12 months if current weight or BMI is documented and weight loss ≥5% of baseline body weight OR ≥5% of baseline BMI is achieved.",
    "Quantity limit (notes only): 9 ml per month.",
    "Remaining gaps: documentation verification, duration, reauthorization response, quantity enforcement and cautions require manual review. PDL status unknown; source is silent."
  ],
